<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingisepp</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yamburg, Yam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kingisepp is a town in Leningrad Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the Luga River. It began as Yam, a stone fortress built by Novgorod in 1384 to guard its north-western frontier. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> held it, as Jama, in 1581–1590 and from 1612 until Russia retook it in 1703 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>. It was renamed Yamburg in the 18th century and Kingisepp in 1922.</p></div>
